WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.800
Do the Byrdes make it back to Chicago?

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.470
What will happen to Ruth's fortune?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.480
Will Three get his revenge for his family?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.030
Keep watching, because these are the questions
we still need answers to after the "Ozark"

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.030
finale.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.969
For a while, Ruth claims victory over the
Byrdes by taking control of the casino.

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:20.240
She receives the rights that belonged to Darlene
Snell, as well as the family farm.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.500
"Seeing as it's Darlene's land, only feels
right for it to be run by locals."

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.710
It even looks like she might get away with
killing Javi.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.530
But alas, Camila bullies Clare into telling
her who killed her son.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.620
Soon enough, Camila ambushes Ruth outside
her home, and the cartel boss shoots the fiery

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.800
fan favorite in the final hour.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.949
This death introduces a major question: What
will happen to Ruth's possessions, such as

00:00:41.949 --> 00:00:45.489
her stake in the casino, the Snell farm, and
the Lazy-O Motel?

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:48.739
Though this might not seem substantial in
the grand scheme of things, the cartel has

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:53.239
used the casino to launder money, despite
Ruth and Rachel Garrison's desire to go clean.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:57.089
It seems likely that Three Langmore will gain
the rights to Ruth's possessions unless she's

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:58.800
listed Rachel as a benefactor.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.429
But all of this is based on speculation.

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:04.600
Ruth was, to say the least, wealthy before
her demise.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.909
The show makes a point of spotlighting this,
given where she's from and the fact that her

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:10.320
record is officially clean before her death.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.460
All of that money has got to go somewhere.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.039
Ruth convinces Rachel to come back to the
Missouri Ozarks, a tainted place that has

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:19.060
caused Rachel an enormous amount of pain.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.290
Now that Ruth is dead, Rachel's plan to work
alongside her is kaput.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:27.009
She might decide to stay and make more money
than she ever has by working at the casino,

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:30.700
but it also wouldn't be surprising if Rachel
disappeared yet again, out of fear.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.880
Perhaps she, Baby Zeke, and Three will flee
town together?

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.090
It's pretty much anyone's guess.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.420
It's also not out of the question that Rachel
might work for the Byrdes.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.520
That prospective work could take place in
Missouri, Chicago, or somewhere else entirely.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.210
This is based solely on speculation since
her storyline ends with her working at the

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.140
casino on the night of the Byrde Foundation
gala before Ruth is killed.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.340
The authorities would have to suspect Camila
of killing Ruth, but that's yet another mystery

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.329
"Ozark" has left in its wake.

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:02.460
With Ruth's passing, Three is left as the
lone survivor of the Langmore clan.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.200
This is a bit surprising, considering he doesn't
receive as much screen time as many other

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.229
Langmore characters and isn't involved in
the cartel or the Snell business.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.340
Nevertheless, Three lives on.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.480
It remains to be seen what the most underrated
Langmore will do now that Ruth is dead.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.349
Ruth presumably left Three with enough resources
to flee the Ozarks and try to find a more

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:22.030
peaceful life someplace else.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.790
But really, you never know.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.010
It's entirely possible that Three will go
after the cartel once he gets a whiff of who

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.170
killed his cousin.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.319
We can't say for sure, of course.

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:34.690
Like most of these questions, this will remain
up for debate forever, barring spin-off projects

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.940
or particularly revealing interviews with
the creators.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.400
But here's what we do know for certain: Three
witnesses his entire family die while the

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.190
Byrde family is in town.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.379
Whether or not those deaths are linked to
that clan, that's the kind of thing that makes

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:49.690
an impression.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.301
For a while, it seemed like the Byrdes might
not make it out of this show alive, or if

00:02:53.301 --> 00:02:55.890
they did, they would have sustained irreparable
damage.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.760
After all, Marty has to fill in as the head
of the cartel in Mexico, Wendy checks herself

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.490
into a mental health facility in a bid to
get her kids back, and Charlotte and Jonah

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.739
are on the verge of leaving with Wendy's father,
Nathan.

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:08.040
"Big decision.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.210
Take some time with it."

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:16.010
But the Byrdes manage to survive separation,
a car crash, and all the other blood-soaked

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.140
events that flood the series, and even manage
to create a successful foundation in the process,

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.379
thanks to Wendy.

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:24.280
They're now free from the cartel and the FBI.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.819
When we last see the four triumphant family
members, Mel has evidence that will link them

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:31.459
to Ben's death, but then Jonah surprises him
with a shotgun.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:32.780
Classic Jonah.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:36.370
This scene, and the entire series, end with
the sound of a gun going off.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.870
Presumably, this comes from Jonah shooting
Mel.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:43.160
Viewers are faced with a major question: Does
the Byrde family finally go back to Chicago

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.290
in the aftermath of this bloodshed?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.819
Someone will have to run the casino after
Ruth's passing, but returning to Chicago was

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:49.819
always the endgame.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:53.090
Do they fulfill that goal at last?

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.090
The Byrdes still have partial ownership of
the casino, and it wouldn't be out of the

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.230
question for the cartel to continue laundering
money through it, if they even need to, given

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.000
their deal with the FBI.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.849
Though of course, this was always Omar's deal,
and it remains to be seen what Camila plans

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:08.099
on doing as the head of the criminal organization.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:12.290
Regardless, this deal with the FBI is supposed
to clear the Byrdes of any charges, as well

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.910
as settle their debts with the cartel.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:17.931
They should be clear of criminal activity
from this point on, but since the Byrde Foundation

00:04:17.931 --> 00:04:21.660
is still doing business with Clare, who is
doing business with the cartel, who knows

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.510
what lines will be crossed?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.020
Will the Byrdes stay clean?

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.900
Hopefully, but there's a significant chance
they won't.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.750
The cartel's leader is now free to do basically
whatever she wants, as long as she continues

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.720
to cooperate with the FBI.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.250
The series leaves the Byrdes free and clear
from the authorities and the cartel, but they

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.620
definitely might not stay that way.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.780
In the final moments of "Ozark," Jonah points
a shotgun at Mel.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.330
The screen goes black, and the sound of a
shot being fired rings out.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.340
This seems pretty definitive, but the ambiguity
of the moment sparks questions.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.310
When shows or movies don't clearly depict
someone's death, it very well might mean they're

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.419
not actually dead.

00:04:56.419 --> 00:05:01.139
Infamously, "The Sopranos" ends on a similarly
mysterious cut to black, leaving fans to wonder

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:03.650
if Tony Soprano meets his bloody end or not.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.070
"Ozark" is less vague than this ending, though.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.590
While Tony Soprano simply looks up in a diner,
the sound of a gun being fired on "Ozark"

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:14.170
is clear, and Jonah's shotgun is the only
visible weapon in the scene.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:17.190
It feels pretty safe to say that Jonah kills
Mel.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.750
But since it's not shown, fans might always
wonder what happens and theorize accordingly.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:26.167
Perhaps, for example, Maya Miller shows up
and fires her gun before Jonah can pull the trigger.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.800
That might seem wild, but it is possible.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.250
More likely than not, Mel meets his demise
at Jonah's hands, and the Byrdes are free

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.319
to drive off into the sunset.

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:38.430
It's a perfect ending to a captivating crime
drama full of surprises, but it's not the

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.720
only ending fans have to accept.

